WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.329 --> 00:00:06.340
In October of 1347, devastation and disease
came to the shores of Europe.

00:00:06.340 --> 00:00:11.650
Twelve ships from the Black Sea docked at
the port of Messina in Sicily, and as citizens

00:00:11.650 --> 00:00:15.929
waited on the docks to welcome the sailors
home, they were horrified to discover that

00:00:15.929 --> 00:00:19.019
almost everyone aboard the ships had been
lost.

00:00:19.019 --> 00:00:23.940
They were still there, but they had succumbed
to a mysterious illness, their bodies covered

00:00:23.940 --> 00:00:26.750
in terrible black boils.

00:00:26.750 --> 00:00:30.850
Everyone was warned to get away, to let the
authorities clear these ships of death out

00:00:30.850 --> 00:00:33.750
of the harbor, but it was already too late.

00:00:33.750 --> 00:00:36.270
The Black Death had arrived.

00:00:36.270 --> 00:00:41.070
The people of Europe had heard rumors, whispers
of a Great Pestilence working its way through

00:00:41.070 --> 00:00:47.190
the trade routes of the East, leaving desolation
in its wake as it raged through China, India,

00:00:47.190 --> 00:00:48.899
Persia, and Syria.

00:00:48.899 --> 00:00:55.480
There were stories of swollen boils under
the armpits, of fever, chills, aches and pains,

00:00:55.480 --> 00:00:58.120
and, before long...death.

00:00:58.120 --> 00:01:02.870
The illness worked so swiftly a man could
go to bed the picture of perfect health and

00:01:02.870 --> 00:01:04.059
be dead by morning.

00:01:04.059 --> 00:01:10.270
Now, this same pestilence had landed in the
harbor and come up onto land, and the invisible

00:01:10.270 --> 00:01:14.689
hand of death and sickness had a grip on everyone's
throats.

00:01:14.689 --> 00:01:19.799
Shortly after the plague's arrival in Italy,
it spread to the port of Marseilles in France,

00:01:19.799 --> 00:01:26.090
then continued on to Rome, Florence, Paris,
Bordeaux, Lyon, and London.

00:01:26.090 --> 00:01:31.890
As the pestilence continued its uncontrollable
spread, people everywhere were terrified.

00:01:31.890 --> 00:01:36.899
Something was invading their homes and taking
their loved ones, and they had no idea what

00:01:36.899 --> 00:01:40.130
was causing it, or how to treat it.

00:01:40.130 --> 00:01:44.939
Some doctors believed that the disease was
caused by miasma, foul-smelling air that carried

00:01:44.939 --> 00:01:46.979
the plague on its breeze.

00:01:46.979 --> 00:01:51.590
Others believed it to be a spiritual sickness,
spread when the airborne spirit of a sick

00:01:51.590 --> 00:01:56.460
man floated out of his eyes and attacked a
healthy person unfortunate enough to make

00:01:56.460 --> 00:01:58.250
eye contact with him.

00:01:58.250 --> 00:02:03.670
Others thought it must be divine punishment,
God's answer to the relentless sins of mankind.

00:02:03.670 --> 00:02:09.640
Amidst the chaos and mistrust, the finger-pointing
and desperate attempts to find something,

00:02:09.640 --> 00:02:15.019
anything to blame, doctors did their best
to treat patients with the limited information

00:02:15.019 --> 00:02:16.209
they had.

00:02:16.209 --> 00:02:20.690
Proposed cures ranged from the useless and
ridiculous to the downright dangerous.

00:02:20.690 --> 00:02:25.160
Some physicians prescribed bloodletting, pricking
open veins to let the disease flow out of

00:02:25.160 --> 00:02:30.050
a patient's body, along with most of the blood
they needed to stay alive.

00:02:30.050 --> 00:02:35.081
Others had the sick take baths in vinegar
and rosewater, which wouldn't harm them, but

00:02:35.081 --> 00:02:38.240
did little to stop the progress of the disease.

00:02:38.240 --> 00:02:42.970
Some cures were expensive, calling for an
emerald to be ground into powder and mixed

00:02:42.970 --> 00:02:44.800
into a glass of wine.

00:02:44.800 --> 00:02:49.480
Other treatments were honestly a fate worse
than simple death, and included drinking one's

00:02:49.480 --> 00:02:56.750
own urine, ingesting snakeskin and precious
metals, and drinking the pus from lanced boils.

00:02:56.750 --> 00:03:01.390
Working with plague patients was a potentially
deadly undertaking, and the few doctors brave

00:03:01.390 --> 00:03:06.280
enough to take on the task needed to take
as many precautions as possible.

00:03:06.280 --> 00:03:12.190
They were outfitted with a specialized uniform:
an ankle-length overcoat, gloves, boots, and

00:03:12.190 --> 00:03:15.250
a bird-like mask ending in a pointed beak.

00:03:15.250 --> 00:03:20.700
The mask contained a rudimentary respirator-like
device filled with dried flowers and herbs,

00:03:20.700 --> 00:03:23.799
spices, camphor, or a vinegar sponge.

00:03:23.799 --> 00:03:29.129
They believed that, by overpowering any potential
bad smells, the scented mask would protect

00:03:29.129 --> 00:03:31.220
against the diseased air.

00:03:31.220 --> 00:03:35.980
The costume included a wide-brimmed leather
hat, and a wooden cane used to examine patients

00:03:35.980 --> 00:03:37.530
without touching them.

00:03:37.530 --> 00:03:42.909
All in all, a plague doctor's attire was easily
recognizable, and more than a little ominous

00:03:42.909 --> 00:03:44.129
in appearance.

00:03:44.129 --> 00:03:49.390
However, what might be unsettling to see today,
or even a signifier of an especially dangerous

00:03:49.390 --> 00:03:55.069
and misguided humanoid anomaly contained by
the SCP Foundation, was once a symbol of hope

00:03:55.069 --> 00:03:56.450
in a dark time.

00:03:56.450 --> 00:04:02.480
Seeing a man enter town in a long dark coat,
a leather hat, and a birdlike mask meant that,

00:04:02.480 --> 00:04:04.879
perhaps, all was not yet lost.

00:04:04.879 --> 00:04:09.650
And so, as news traveled about a mysterious
illness stealing souls in the night, turning

00:04:09.650 --> 00:04:14.130
their bodies into masses of infectious boils
that needed to be rounded up and burned in

00:04:14.130 --> 00:04:18.940
pits outside of town, the people of a tiny
French village were anxiously awaiting the

00:04:18.940 --> 00:04:21.900
arrival of one such Plague Doctor.

00:04:21.900 --> 00:04:25.970
They hoped a physician would arrive before
the first person fell ill, but they could

00:04:25.970 --> 00:04:29.100
feel the cloud of illness creeping ever closer.

00:04:29.100 --> 00:04:33.590
It was a joyful day when, one morning, a young
man ran through the town square, banging a

00:04:33.590 --> 00:04:36.940
pot and a pan together and crying out: "A
doctor is here!

00:04:36.940 --> 00:04:39.150
A doctor has come to town!"

00:04:39.150 --> 00:04:44.550
Indeed, just behind the young man came a stranger,
dressed in long black robes and wearing a

00:04:44.550 --> 00:04:46.009
wide-brimmed hat.

00:04:46.009 --> 00:04:51.020
However, instead of the beaked mask, this
man's face was covered in a rather curious

00:04:51.020 --> 00:04:52.020
manner.

00:04:52.020 --> 00:04:57.009
He wore a white porcelain mask, frozen in
a permanent smile.

00:04:57.009 --> 00:05:01.400
Behind the eyes and open mouth, the villagers
could see only darkness.

00:05:01.400 --> 00:05:05.220
This must, they thought, be some sort of new
preventative measure, some protective gear

00:05:05.220 --> 00:05:09.810
he had brought with him from whatever medically
advanced city he had just been in.

00:05:09.810 --> 00:05:13.389
Still, before getting their hopes up, the
people wanted to be sure.

00:05:13.389 --> 00:05:14.560
"Excuse me."

00:05:14.560 --> 00:05:18.900
An older farmer, a respected pillar of the
community, approached the masked man.

00:05:18.900 --> 00:05:21.160
"Are you a physician?"

00:05:21.160 --> 00:05:23.400
"Indeed, I am!"

00:05:23.400 --> 00:05:24.900
The stranger replied cheerfully.

00:05:24.900 --> 00:05:29.570
"I have reason to believe the Black Death
will shortly come to this little town, and

00:05:29.570 --> 00:05:34.300
I was sent here to provide my services to
anyone who may need them."

00:05:34.300 --> 00:05:39.150
In case there was any question about his identity,
he produced from his side a large doctor's

00:05:39.150 --> 00:05:44.060
bag, filled with tinctures and tools, with
rags soaked in vinegar and vials of ground-up

00:05:44.060 --> 00:05:45.900
eggshells and saffron.

00:05:45.900 --> 00:05:50.300
The townspeople couldn't help but feel lucky
that such a well-equipped physician had come

00:05:50.300 --> 00:05:54.510
to their town, to arm them with the tools
they needed to combat the plague.

00:05:54.510 --> 00:06:00.160
Later that day, their fortunes seemed to double
when yet another stranger strode into town.

00:06:00.160 --> 00:06:04.150
This man was dressed far more traditionally,
in the garb the people had come to expect

00:06:04.150 --> 00:06:06.729
from a physician tasked with treating the
Black Death.

00:06:06.729 --> 00:06:12.710
The man was dressed in long dark robes, leather
gloves, boots, and a beaked mask.

00:06:12.710 --> 00:06:15.840
He carried a bag, similar to that of the first
doctor.

00:06:15.840 --> 00:06:21.190
The same older farmer approached the doctor,
curious to see two newcomers on the same day.

00:06:21.190 --> 00:06:24.900
He couldn't remember the last time he saw
so many strangers arriving in their little

00:06:24.900 --> 00:06:26.180
hamlet at the same time.

00:06:26.180 --> 00:06:28.450
"Have you come to help us, Doctor?"

00:06:28.450 --> 00:06:29.450
He asked.

00:06:29.450 --> 00:06:31.050
"Fear not, my good fellow.

00:06:31.050 --> 00:06:32.050
I have.

00:06:32.050 --> 00:06:37.190
I am here to fight the Great Pestilence, and
I will lend you all of my effort and years

00:06:37.190 --> 00:06:38.320
of medical knowledge.

00:06:38.320 --> 00:06:41.000
Tell me, are there any infected yet?

00:06:41.000 --> 00:06:43.080
I would be happy to treat them."

00:06:43.080 --> 00:06:44.210
The farmer shook his head.

00:06:44.210 --> 00:06:46.380
"We are all healthy here, Sir.

00:06:46.380 --> 00:06:50.840
But it is fortuitous indeed, to have two great
physicians here to aid us in these troubling

00:06:50.840 --> 00:06:51.840
times."

00:06:51.840 --> 00:06:54.169
The Doctor tilted his head to the side, perplexed.

00:06:54.169 --> 00:06:55.169
"Two?

00:06:55.169 --> 00:06:57.370
I assure you, I am traveling quite alone."

00:06:57.370 --> 00:06:59.910
"The man who arrived before you!"

00:06:59.910 --> 00:07:00.910
The farmer insisted.

00:07:00.910 --> 00:07:04.580
"Come and meet him, I'm sure you two will
have a lot to talk about."

00:07:04.580 --> 00:07:09.210
More than a little confused, the Plague Doctor
followed the farmer to the town's tavern,

00:07:09.210 --> 00:07:14.060
where he was ushered to a table that had one
occupant: the man in the white mask.

00:07:14.060 --> 00:07:19.069
He greeted the Doctor with that frozen porcelain
smile, and a tone that was filled with mannered

00:07:19.069 --> 00:07:20.150
congeniality.

00:07:20.150 --> 00:07:22.560
"Ah, another Doctor!

00:07:22.560 --> 00:07:24.400
Welcome, my dear colleague.

00:07:24.400 --> 00:07:26.930
It will be a pleasure to work with you."

00:07:26.930 --> 00:07:30.319
The Plague Doctor sat across from the Mask,
and stared at him inquisitively.

00:07:30.319 --> 00:07:36.070
"I was unaware there would be another physician
in town, please forgive my confusion."

00:07:36.070 --> 00:07:37.949
"Not to worry!"

00:07:37.949 --> 00:07:41.840
The Mask's smile seemed to widen, though of
course that was impossible.

00:07:41.840 --> 00:07:45.600
"It will be a relief to have someone else
to share the burden.

00:07:45.600 --> 00:07:48.090
I am certain we will work together quite well."

00:07:48.090 --> 00:07:52.770
"Tell me," The Plague Doctor began, "How did
you come to hear of the need for a doctor

00:07:52.770 --> 00:07:53.870
in this town?

00:07:53.870 --> 00:07:57.780
It is my understanding that none have fallen
ill thus far."

00:07:57.780 --> 00:07:59.400
"Rumors, that is all.

00:07:59.400 --> 00:08:03.240
And in times such as these, one can never
be too careful.

00:08:03.240 --> 00:08:06.220
After all, we took an oath to help those in
need, did we not?"

00:08:06.220 --> 00:08:10.520
The Plague Doctor couldn't place why, but
he felt strangely apprehensive about this

00:08:10.520 --> 00:08:12.710
fellow in the white mask.

00:08:12.710 --> 00:08:17.569
Something about him did not seem quite right,
from his untraditional choice of attire, to

00:08:17.569 --> 00:08:22.590
the rustling sound inside of the man's bag,
to the strange droplets of something black

00:08:22.590 --> 00:08:25.240
that had gathered on the table in front of
him.

00:08:25.240 --> 00:08:28.680
Still, perhaps the exhaustion of his journey
had put him on edge.

00:08:28.680 --> 00:08:33.430
Many hands make for lighter work, and he should
be grateful for the assistance promised.

00:08:33.430 --> 00:08:37.729
He was used to working alone, but he would
simply have to adjust.

00:08:37.729 --> 00:08:42.990
Besides, it was entirely possible no one would
become ill at all, and the letter he had received

00:08:42.990 --> 00:08:47.700
summoning him to the town was based on inaccurate
assessments of the area's risk.

00:08:47.700 --> 00:08:53.470
He would stay a fortnight, evaluate the health
of the people, and, if nothing of import arose,

00:08:53.470 --> 00:08:58.790
he would travel onward to the next town and
continue his endless battle against the Pestilence.

00:08:58.790 --> 00:09:02.980
But before that fortnight could pass, someone
did fall ill.

00:09:02.980 --> 00:09:06.890
The old farmer's wife ran to the tavern in
the early hours of the morning, only two days

00:09:06.890 --> 00:09:09.019
after the Doctors came to town.

00:09:09.019 --> 00:09:12.970
The Plague Doctor was already awake when she
arrived, sipping a cup of tea and eating a

00:09:12.970 --> 00:09:15.140
piece of toasted bread with butter.

00:09:15.140 --> 00:09:18.930
She begged him to leave his breakfast and
come inspect her husband immediately.

00:09:18.930 --> 00:09:23.750
Her husband had collapsed while milking the
cows, and nothing she did could wake him.

00:09:23.750 --> 00:09:27.090
His forehead felt hot to the touch, slick
with sweat.

00:09:27.090 --> 00:09:30.750
As he looked, the Plague Doctor could see
that the farmer's body was covered in the

00:09:30.750 --> 00:09:34.450
tell-tale boils that he had seen so many times
before.

00:09:34.450 --> 00:09:38.500
He instructed the woman to stand back, to
stay away from her husband lest she catch

00:09:38.500 --> 00:09:39.500
his sickness.

00:09:39.500 --> 00:09:43.820
Then, he began a thorough inspection, using
his cane to lift the man's arms and check

00:09:43.820 --> 00:09:44.820
beneath them.

00:09:44.820 --> 00:09:47.170
Sure enough, there were more boils there.

00:09:47.170 --> 00:09:48.840
"Your husband is very ill."

00:09:48.840 --> 00:09:50.380
He told the weeping woman.

00:09:50.380 --> 00:09:53.810
"But I assure you, Madame, I will do my best
to make him well.

00:09:53.810 --> 00:09:56.250
We will begin by letting the blood from these
areas."

00:09:56.250 --> 00:09:58.950
He pulled a scalpel from his bag, and began
the procedure.

00:09:58.950 --> 00:10:04.490
"This will release the humors that have gathered
in excess, and allow his body to regain balance."

00:10:04.490 --> 00:10:06.160
"It will not work."

00:10:06.160 --> 00:10:11.080
A voice behind him disturbed his careful work,
and the Plague Doctor turned around, to see

00:10:11.080 --> 00:10:13.370
the white-masked man watching him from the
doorway.

00:10:13.370 --> 00:10:15.060
"I beg your pardon?"

00:10:15.060 --> 00:10:16.350
The Plague Doctor straightened.

00:10:16.350 --> 00:10:18.440
"This man needs a different cure.

00:10:18.440 --> 00:10:20.290
Please, allow me to treat him."

00:10:20.290 --> 00:10:23.840
The Plague Doctor hesitated, uncertain about
having his methods questioned.

00:10:23.840 --> 00:10:28.209
But the pleading cries of the farmer's wife
persuaded him to step back and allow his colleague

00:10:28.209 --> 00:10:29.550
to try his own treatment.

00:10:29.550 --> 00:10:32.149
"Very well, I will let you work."

00:10:32.149 --> 00:10:35.740
The Plague Doctor left the room to give the
white-masked man some privacy.

00:10:35.740 --> 00:10:39.680
The farmer's wife joined him, and the two
sat in the front room of the house, waiting

00:10:39.680 --> 00:10:42.300
for whatever news the other doctor might bring.

00:10:42.300 --> 00:10:44.130
Finally, after many hours, he returned.

00:10:44.130 --> 00:10:46.370
"I am very sorry."

00:10:46.370 --> 00:10:50.660
The man's white mask now bore the expression
of a deep, sorrowful frown.

00:10:50.660 --> 00:10:52.630
His gloved hands were covered with blood.

00:10:52.630 --> 00:10:55.610
"Your husband's condition was far too advanced.

00:10:55.610 --> 00:10:59.870
If I had arrived sooner to treat him, and
if his blood had not been let so hastily by

00:10:59.870 --> 00:11:02.420
my colleague, perhaps I would have saved him.

00:11:02.420 --> 00:11:04.399
But he is with the angels now."

00:11:04.399 --> 00:11:09.339
The woman began to cry again, and as she wiped
her eyes, the Plague Doctor noticed the masked

00:11:09.339 --> 00:11:15.190
man do the same, wiping something thick and
black from the eye holes of his mask.

00:11:15.190 --> 00:11:16.190
Strange.

00:11:16.190 --> 00:11:19.959
And then there were the words he had said,
words that offended the Doctor to his very

00:11:19.959 --> 00:11:20.959
core.

00:11:20.959 --> 00:11:24.700
"Are you implying I am to be held responsible
for this lost patient?"

00:11:24.700 --> 00:11:25.700
He demanded.

00:11:25.700 --> 00:11:28.630
"Of course not, it was the Plague that took
his life.

00:11:28.630 --> 00:11:32.300
But...well, we will never know exactly what
might have happened if I had arrived to treat

00:11:32.300 --> 00:11:33.540
him first.

00:11:33.540 --> 00:11:37.490
Never mind, best not to dwell on such hypothetical
matters."

00:11:37.490 --> 00:11:41.360
The white-masked man held out a cup to the
grieving widow, filled with something dark

00:11:41.360 --> 00:11:42.360
and viscous.

00:11:42.360 --> 00:11:46.370
"My dear lady, in caring for your husband
you were exposed to his sickness.

00:11:46.370 --> 00:11:50.330
You will take ill and follow him into death
if you do not take care to prevent the plague

00:11:50.330 --> 00:11:51.649
from taking in you.

00:11:51.649 --> 00:11:53.160
Please, drink this.

00:11:53.160 --> 00:11:54.730
It will keep you safe."

00:11:54.730 --> 00:11:58.740
Before the Plague Doctor could ask what the
unfamiliar medicine was, the woman had already

00:11:58.740 --> 00:12:03.080
taken the cup with trembling hands, and drank
its contents in one swallow.

00:12:03.080 --> 00:12:06.040
"Please do call on me if anything else troubles
you.

00:12:06.040 --> 00:12:08.100
My condolences for your loss."

00:12:08.100 --> 00:12:11.089
And with that, the white-masked man was gone.

00:12:11.089 --> 00:12:15.520
The farmer was the first citizen to succumb
to the Black Plague, but sadly, he would not

00:12:15.520 --> 00:12:16.820
be the last.

00:12:16.820 --> 00:12:21.430
Once the disease had its hooks in the town,
it was going to be difficult to root it out.

00:12:21.430 --> 00:12:26.329
In spite of taking the strange curative drink,
the farmer's wife was lost only a few days

00:12:26.329 --> 00:12:27.329
later.

00:12:27.329 --> 00:12:31.790
All throughout the town, more and more grew
ill, and it seemed there was no relief in

00:12:31.790 --> 00:12:32.790
sight.

00:12:32.790 --> 00:12:36.070
The Plague Doctor did his best to treat the
patients as they came, providing them with

00:12:36.070 --> 00:12:41.449
homemade tinctures of herbs and wild mushrooms,
cleaning their wounds with distilled spirits,

00:12:41.449 --> 00:12:43.610
bathing them in the purest of vinegar.

00:12:43.610 --> 00:12:48.339
He even resorted to some of his more experimental
treatments, those his colleagues in Paris

00:12:48.339 --> 00:12:54.470
had questioned, had dismissed as far too close
to the occult and far too removed from science.

00:12:54.470 --> 00:12:58.990
He took the blood from a healthy cow and attempted
to transmit it into a human patient.

00:12:58.990 --> 00:13:03.160
He deliberately stopped the heart and then
started it again with the venom of an exotic

00:13:03.160 --> 00:13:04.160
snake.

00:13:04.160 --> 00:13:06.520
Still, he was unable to save any of them.

00:13:06.520 --> 00:13:11.190
He was beginning to lose faith in himself,
and the people of the village were following

00:13:11.190 --> 00:13:12.190
suit.

00:13:12.190 --> 00:13:15.870
Slowly, the families of the sick were beginning
to bring their loved ones to the man in the

00:13:15.870 --> 00:13:19.850
white mask instead, trusting only him to help
them.

00:13:19.850 --> 00:13:22.660
And, somehow, help them he did.

00:13:22.660 --> 00:13:26.470
The Plague Doctor couldn't be sure what the
white-masked man was doing.

00:13:26.470 --> 00:13:31.230
His supposed colleague was secretive about
his methods, never allowing himself to be

00:13:31.230 --> 00:13:32.230
observed.

00:13:32.230 --> 00:13:36.770
He would not leave his makeshift workshop,
a room in the attic of the tavern where he

00:13:36.770 --> 00:13:38.170
saw his patients.

00:13:38.170 --> 00:13:42.440
But, whatever he was doing must have worked,
because for every one of his losses, there

00:13:42.440 --> 00:13:47.839
was a person whose fever broke, whose skin
miraculously cleared of blemishes, and who

00:13:47.839 --> 00:13:50.930
returned home to their life just as it was
before.

00:13:50.930 --> 00:13:53.360
The Plague Doctor couldn't understand it,
any of it.

00:13:53.360 --> 00:13:56.380
He had cured patients before, he knew he had.

00:13:56.380 --> 00:14:00.279
His successes had been renowned throughout
the land, had earned him commendations from

00:14:00.279 --> 00:14:01.760
generals and kings.

00:14:01.760 --> 00:14:07.680
But now, here, ever since he met this new
doctor in the eerie white mask, something

00:14:07.680 --> 00:14:10.370
was terribly wrong with his work.

00:14:10.370 --> 00:14:13.470
Perhaps the other doctor would allow him to
assist, to learn from him.

00:14:13.470 --> 00:14:18.220
In his current sorry state, Plague Doctor
could only hope to become the assistant of

00:14:18.220 --> 00:14:19.220
a great man.

00:14:19.220 --> 00:14:23.480
Once he had absorbed some of his knowledge,
perhaps then he could return to his former

00:14:23.480 --> 00:14:26.279
state, do as much good as he once had.

00:14:26.279 --> 00:14:30.280
One evening after he finished his supper of
vegetable soup and crusty bread, the Plague

00:14:30.280 --> 00:14:35.410
Doctor summoned his courage and decided to
go upstairs and pay the masked man a visit.

00:14:35.410 --> 00:14:39.509
As he lifted his fist to knock on the door,
he could hear muffled voices coming from the

00:14:39.509 --> 00:14:40.580
other side.

00:14:40.580 --> 00:14:45.220
He was not ordinarily one to eavesdrop, but
something in the tone of the conversation

00:14:45.220 --> 00:14:47.769
made him hesitate and listen for a moment.

00:14:47.769 --> 00:14:50.470
"I am afraid you might be right."

00:14:50.470 --> 00:14:51.470
The Mask said.

00:14:51.470 --> 00:14:53.690
"There is something unusual about the other
Doctor.

00:14:53.690 --> 00:14:59.220
I do not wish to cast aspersions, but...it
seems as if the Plague only began to appear

00:14:59.220 --> 00:15:01.170
here once he arrived in town."

00:15:01.170 --> 00:15:04.900
"Do you think...he brought the disease with
him?"

00:15:04.900 --> 00:15:07.820
The other voice, belonging to the local judge,
replied.

00:15:07.820 --> 00:15:10.880
"I am sorry to say that I do."

00:15:10.880 --> 00:15:12.730
"What can be done to stop this?

00:15:12.730 --> 00:15:14.949
To drive the Plague out of our community?"

00:15:14.949 --> 00:15:15.949
The judge asked.

00:15:15.949 --> 00:15:18.690
"In my opinion, there is only one choice.

00:15:18.690 --> 00:15:20.500
The Doctor must leave this town.

00:15:20.500 --> 00:15:25.130
By choice or by force, dead or alive...that
will be up to him."

00:15:25.130 --> 00:15:28.209
The Plague Doctor clapped a hand over his
beak in shock.

00:15:28.209 --> 00:15:29.880
Conspiracy against him?

00:15:29.880 --> 00:15:30.880
But why?!

00:15:30.880 --> 00:15:34.570
He could hear rustling on the other side of
the door, someone preparing to open it.

00:15:34.570 --> 00:15:36.670
He must hide before they spotted him!

00:15:36.670 --> 00:15:40.580
He ducked into a closet, shutting the door
behind him, and tucked himself away in the

00:15:40.580 --> 00:15:43.500
dark as the judge's footsteps passed by outside.

00:15:43.500 --> 00:15:45.090
Finally, it fell silent.

00:15:45.090 --> 00:15:49.620
With a sigh of relief, the Plague Doctor pushed
open the closet door.

00:15:49.620 --> 00:15:53.500
But there, waiting for him, was that unmoving
pale white face.

00:15:53.500 --> 00:15:57.290
This time, it was smiling, a malicious, gleeful
smile.

00:15:57.290 --> 00:15:59.600
"Oh, hello, Doctor."

00:15:59.600 --> 00:16:01.130
The Masked Man said.

00:16:01.130 --> 00:16:04.500
His words were polite, but his voice was cruel
and cold.

00:16:04.500 --> 00:16:06.079
"What have you done?

00:16:06.079 --> 00:16:09.019
Why would you tell the people such slanderous
lies?"

00:16:09.019 --> 00:16:10.620
The Plague Doctor demanded.

00:16:10.620 --> 00:16:11.620
"Simple.

00:16:11.620 --> 00:16:19.440
They need someone to blame, and I won't have
it be me."

00:16:19.440 --> 00:16:22.110
The Masked man laughed then, a hollow sound.

00:16:22.110 --> 00:16:25.050
"Haven't you figured it out, Doctor?

00:16:25.050 --> 00:16:28.769
Haven't your brilliant deductive skills led
you to the answer?

00:16:28.769 --> 00:16:33.970
Why your cures have done nothing, why all
of your patients perish while so many of mine

00:16:33.970 --> 00:16:34.970
thrive?"

00:16:34.970 --> 00:16:37.019
"...You made them ill?

00:16:37.019 --> 00:16:38.019
Deliberately?

00:16:38.019 --> 00:16:39.610
But how?

00:16:39.610 --> 00:16:40.610
And why?"

00:16:40.610 --> 00:16:42.769
The Plague Doctor gaped in shock and horror.

00:16:42.769 --> 00:16:46.750
"The how is for me to know and take to the
grave.

00:16:46.750 --> 00:16:48.610
But as for the why...

00:16:48.610 --> 00:16:53.750
I'd be happy to tell you, because no one will
believe a word you say.

00:16:53.750 --> 00:16:58.329
I intend to rule this town, the first of many
I will make my domain.

00:16:58.329 --> 00:17:04.039
And there is no way to inspire loyalty in
a population like freeing them from the grip

00:17:04.039 --> 00:17:06.050
of the Black Death.

00:17:06.050 --> 00:17:09.059
Unfortunate that you had to arrive and complicate
my plans.

00:17:09.059 --> 00:17:18.079
But you will soon be taken care of, and then
I will have nothing more to worry about."

00:17:18.079 --> 00:17:21.480
The Mask cackled again, triumphant and wicked.

00:17:21.480 --> 00:17:23.150
"You VILLAIN!"

00:17:23.150 --> 00:17:26.799
The Plague Doctor roared, grabbing at the
man's robes and trying to yank him close enough

00:17:26.799 --> 00:17:27.799
to fight.

00:17:27.799 --> 00:17:32.500
He could not get a grip on the man, but the
robes came loose and fell to the ground, revealing

00:17:32.500 --> 00:17:34.100
a horrible sight.

00:17:34.100 --> 00:17:38.020
Where there should have been a man, flesh
and blood and beating heart, there was nothing

00:17:38.020 --> 00:17:41.929
but a skeleton, dripping black slime onto
the floor.

00:17:41.929 --> 00:17:47.250
The mask covered a face of bone and desiccated
skin, the body underneath a rattling marionette

00:17:47.250 --> 00:17:50.270
propelled by unnatural, evil forces.

00:17:50.270 --> 00:17:54.720
It was too much for the Plague Doctor to take,
and he did the only thing he could think to

00:17:54.720 --> 00:17:57.480
do: he turned, and he ran.

00:17:57.480 --> 00:18:02.740
The Plague Doctor grabbed his cane, his trusty
apothecary bag, and ran out into the streets.

00:18:02.740 --> 00:18:03.740
"Please!"

00:18:03.740 --> 00:18:04.740
He cried out into the night.

00:18:04.740 --> 00:18:05.740
"Listen to me!

00:18:05.740 --> 00:18:07.740
You have been fooled by a Devil!

00:18:07.740 --> 00:18:09.659
He brings desolation, not the cure!

00:18:09.659 --> 00:18:11.370
He is the sickness!"

00:18:11.370 --> 00:18:13.190
"You're a madman!"

00:18:13.190 --> 00:18:17.230
The judge cried, brandishing a flaming torch
in one hand, a pitchfork in the other.

00:18:17.230 --> 00:18:22.020
"You brought death to our town, and now you
spout lies about our savior!"

00:18:22.020 --> 00:18:24.370
"Please, my dear fellow, hear me!

00:18:24.370 --> 00:18:26.490
You are not safe here!"

00:18:26.490 --> 00:18:27.799
The Plague Doctor begged.

00:18:27.799 --> 00:18:31.640
The judge lunged at him with the pitchfork,
and, forgetting to touch the man with his

00:18:31.640 --> 00:18:35.710
cane, the Plague Doctor grabbed his arm with
his own hand to stop the assault.

00:18:35.710 --> 00:18:39.760
The judge's eyes went wide, and he dropped
to the ground in a lifeless heap.

00:18:39.760 --> 00:18:40.980
"He killed him!"

00:18:40.980 --> 00:18:42.090
Cried a bystander.

00:18:42.090 --> 00:18:44.500
"The false doctor is a murderer!"

00:18:44.500 --> 00:18:49.240
As the Plague Doctor watched, an angry mob
descended on him, waving their torches and

00:18:49.240 --> 00:18:50.240
weapons.

00:18:50.240 --> 00:18:53.140
They would not hear reason, they would not
listen.

00:18:53.140 --> 00:18:54.980
He would have to flee.

00:18:54.980 --> 00:18:58.840
The Plague Doctor ran until the cries of angry
townspeople and the glow of their torches

00:18:58.840 --> 00:19:00.980
had faded into dark and silence.

00:19:00.980 --> 00:19:03.010
And then he ran some more.

00:19:03.010 --> 00:19:07.650
He ran all the way to a neighboring town,
where he told stories of a shambling corpse

00:19:07.650 --> 00:19:13.220
in a white porcelain mask, bringing a Plague
of illness and deception, and could only hope

00:19:13.220 --> 00:19:16.470
and pray that these people would listen.

00:19:16.470 --> 00:19:24.080
Now go check out “When Day Breaks SCP-049”
and “SCP-001 - Can SCP-049 Finally Cure

00:19:24.080 --> 00:19:25.270
When Day Breaks?”

00:19:25.270 --> 00:19:28.040
for more battles of wits between the Plague
Doctor and the diabolical possessive mask!

